  "explanation": {
    "short": "Four vowel signs sit above the letter. One stroke is e (े, as in मेरा) and two strokes is ai (ै, as in है, कैसे). The curved stroke with a bar is o (ो, as in को) and a bar with two strokes is au (ौ, as in कौन).",
    "more": "ै sounds like the \"a\" in \"hat\" followed by a little \"i\"; ौ is like \"aw\" followed by a little \"u\". े and ो are pure single sounds. Count the strokes on the letter: one is e or o, two is ai or au."
  },
